# Legacy Cursor Rules Template
#
# `.cursorrules` remains available for older Cursor versions. New projects should
# use native Agent Skills plus `.cursor/rules/sk-skills.mdc` or `AGENTS.md`.

## Public Skills

- `/sk-team-feature` — Discovery → optional Research → Planning → optional
  Documentation Review → Testing → Implementation → Code Review → Acceptance →
  Retrospective → Archive.
- `/sk-team-quick` — Architect → Developer → Review → Acceptance.
- `/sk-team-status` — Show active workflow state.
- `/sk-team-help` — Show workflow documentation.
- `/sk-onboard` — Discover the project and generate navigation/convention profiles.
- `/sk-discover-project` — Map structure, stack, domains, and API surface.
- `/sk-explore-codebase` — Generate navigation and project convention profiles.
- `/sk-plan-mode` — Create and approve a structured implementation plan.
- `/sk-code-review` — Review committed, staged, unstaged, and untracked changes.
- `/sk-explore-codestyle` — Derive authoritative project coding conventions.
- `/sk-copy-context` — Copy the current session context for handoff.

## Internal Roles

- `sk-product-analyst`
- `sk-researcher`
- `sk-architect`
- `sk-doc-reviewer`
- `sk-tester`
- `sk-developer`
- `sk-review-orchestrator`
- `sk-acceptance-reviewer`

Active feature artifacts live under `openspec/changes/<feature-name>/`. Approved
workflows are archived under `openspec/completed/<feature-name>/`.
